  "note": "First election of the Antrim Town Commissioners under the 1922 wards, polled Monday 15 January 1923. Nine candidates were nominated for the nine seats and were declared elected without a contest (Belfast News-Letter, 6 January 1923, p. 6). Names image-read in the News-Letter and the Northern Whig of 6 Jan 1923 (same report): 'Messrs. F. T. Smith, J.P.; R. Mullan, John M'Cabe, W. D. M'Keown, Thos. M'Master, Jas. Baird, Jas. Christie, Chas. Burrowes, and Jas. Wilson. Messrs. S. Brennan, J.P., and W. W. M'Fetridge (who has left Antrim) did not seek re-election'. Corrected (gap-fill 6 Nov 2026) from an earlier reading R. Millar, W. J. M'Kerwin and Thomas M'Mullan; the 1926 list (BNL 7 Jan 1926 p. 8) has Richard Mullan and William M'Keown. Returned unopposed."
